WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
After a major burn, fluid shifts out of the

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:04.497
circulation and tissue edema develops.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.020
Watch fluid collect outside
the vessel while the circulating

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:08.920
supply falls.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.793
Visible swelling does not prove adequate blood volume.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.970
Fluid replacement supports the
circulation; increasing capillary permeability is

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:18.811
not its purpose.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.320
The supplied deck identifies urine output as the most

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.926
reliable resuscitation measure.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.910
Capillary seal marks the end of burn shock in

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.397
this source.
